<section id="about" class="why"><div class="w">
  <h2>About ICCE</h2>
  <p class="sub" style="max-width:70ch">ICCE is one of the leading organisations in education. ICCE is in tune with the latest trends in technology, thus setting the highest standards of computer education for students.</p>
  <p class="sub" style="max-width:70ch">ICCE provides learners with one of the most comprehensive yet extended ranges of training options, with something for virtually every segment of society. In line with its vision of bringing people and computers together, ICCE has built up a broad portfolio of computer training programs, from simple, short-term courses for first-time users to advanced, high-tech offerings for professionals looking at re-skilling or upgrading their knowledge.</p>

  <div class="mission"><span>Our Mission</span><p>Every student, even the most underprivileged, deserves a good computer education. ICCE was started to provide quality computer education at the lowest possible fees.</p></div>
</div></section>

<section id="courses"><div class="w">
  <h2>Our Courses</h2>
  <p class="sub">Tap any course to see full details. Contact us for duration and fees.</p>
  <div class="grid">
<details class="c"><summary><h3>Smart AI</h3><p>Learn to use AI tools in daily work, studies and business.</p></summary><div class="ex"><div style="flex:1 1 340px;min-width:260px"><img src="data:image/jpeg;base64," alt="Smart AI Course at ICCE Computer Education" style="width:100%;height:auto;border-radius:10px;display:block"></div><div class="exp"><b>About this course</b><p>The Smart AI program introduces fundamental concepts and techniques used in artificial intelligence. It typically starts with computer fundamentals and an overview of AI, explaining what it is and how it is applied in various fields.</p><p>Focused on creative tools, students start by learning how AI can help generate content like images, graphics, videos and chatbots. For instance, AI tools like ChatGPT can be used for text-based tasks, such as building conversational chatbots or generating written content. AI-powered platforms like MidJourney let users create images and graphics by simply providing a text prompt, making visual design easier and more accessible. For videos, AI tools like InVideo help with editing, adding effects, or even generating short video clips from a simple script.</p><p>The goal is to understand how AI can assist in creative projects and automate repetitive tasks, enhancing efficiency and creativity.</p></div></div><b>Course syllabus</b><b class="mod">1. Fundamentals of Computers</b><ul><li><strong>Computer hardware &amp; software:</strong> Basics of what makes up a computer (CPU, RAM, storage) and how operating systems and applications function.</li><li><strong>MS Office:</strong> Familiarity with tools like Word, Excel, PowerPoint for productivity tasks.</li><li><strong>Email &amp; Internet:</strong> Understanding of email protocols, internet browsing, and online communication.</li></ul><b class="mod">2. Concepts of Artificial Intelligence</b><ul><li><strong>Generative AI:</strong> AI models that create new data (e.g., text, images) like GPT or DALL-E.</li><li><strong>Types of Generative AI:</strong> Including text generation, image generation, music, and others.</li><li><strong>Natural Language Processing (NLP):</strong> Techniques for machines to understand, interpret, and respond to human language.</li><li><strong>Use of AI in industries:</strong> Exploring how AI transforms sectors like healthcare, finance, entertainment, etc.</li></ul><b class="mod">3. Chat GPT</b><ul><li><strong>Introduction to GPT models:</strong> Understanding how GPT-3/4 works and its use in generating human-like text.</li><li><strong>Overview of NLP and chatbots:</strong> How conversational AI is used to interact with humans.</li><li><strong>Fine-tuning GPT models:</strong> Customizing AI models for specific tasks and applications.</li></ul><b class="mod">4. Midjourney</b><ul><li><strong>Account Setup &amp; Management:</strong> Navigating Midjourney for AI-generated images.</li><li><strong>Prompt Creation:</strong> Learning how to create specific prompts to generate desired images.</li><li><strong>Different Modes &amp; Models:</strong> Exploring Midjourney’s versions and customization options.</li></ul><b class="mod">5. InVideos</b><ul><li><strong>Text-to-Video Mastery:</strong> Transforming text inputs into video outputs.</li><li><strong>Editing Techniques:</strong> Applying video editing skills within InVideo.</li><li><strong>Voice-Over Customization:</strong> Adding and modifying voice-overs for videos.</li><li><strong>Platform Optimization:</strong> Optimizing video content for various platforms like YouTube, social media, etc.</li></ul><b>Who it is for</b><p>Students, job seekers, business owners</p><b>Career options</b><p>Content creator, AI-assisted office work, freelancing</p><a href="#enquiry" data-c="Smart AI">Enquire about this course</a></details>
<details class="c"><summary><h3>Digital Marketing</h3><p>Grow your business or career with social media, ads and online promotion.</p></summary><img src="data:image/jpeg;base64," alt="Digital Marketing course banner, ICCE Computer Education" style="width:100%;height:auto;border-radius:10px;display:block;margin-top:14px"><div class="ex"><div class="exp"><b>About this course</b><p>The Digital Marketing program teaches how businesses find and reach customers online. It starts with computer and internet basics, then covers social media marketing, SEO, paid advertising and content creation.</p><p>Students learn to plan posts, design with Canva, set up business pages and understand how ads on Google, Facebook and Instagram work.</p><p>The goal is to help students promote a business or build a career in digital marketing.</p></div></div><b>Course syllabus</b><b class="mod">1. Fundamentals of Computers &amp; Internet</b><ul><li><strong>Computer basics:</strong> Using a computer, files and folders, typing.</li><li><strong>Email &amp; Internet:</strong> Email, browsing and online communication.</li><li><strong>Online tools:</strong> Google tools and MS Office for daily marketing work.</li></ul><b class="mod">2. Digital Marketing Concepts</b><ul><li><strong>What is digital marketing:</strong> How online marketing works and why businesses need it.</li><li><strong>Target audience:</strong> Finding the right customers for a product or service.</li><li><strong>Online branding:</strong> Building a name and image for a business online.</li></ul><b class="mod">3. Social Media Marketing</b><ul><li><strong>Pages &amp; profiles:</strong> Setting up Facebook and Instagram business pages.</li><li><strong>Content planning:</strong> Planning posts, captions and a posting calendar.</li><li><strong>Reels &amp; short videos:</strong> Creating short videos that people want to watch.</li><li><strong>Engagement:</strong> Replying to customers and growing followers.</li></ul><b class="mod">4. SEO &amp; Website Basics</b><ul><li><strong>SEO basics:</strong> How people find websites on Google, and keywords.</li><li><strong>On-page SEO:</strong> Titles, descriptions and content that rank better.</li><li><strong>Google Business Profile:</strong> Getting a local business listed on Google and Maps.</li></ul><b class="mod">5. Paid Advertising</b><ul><li><strong>Google Ads basics:</strong> Search ads and how they are set up.</li><li><strong>Meta Ads:</strong> Running ads on Facebook and Instagram.</li><li><strong>Budget &amp; targeting:</strong> Choosing audience, budget and reading results.</li></ul><b class="mod">6. Content Creation</b><ul><li><strong>Canva design:</strong> Making posters, banners and social media posts.</li><li><strong>Copywriting:</strong> Writing captions and messages that get replies.</li><li><strong>WhatsApp &amp; email marketing:</strong> Reaching customers directly.</li></ul><b>Who it is for</b><p>Students, shop owners, freelancers</p><b>Career options</b><p>Digital marketer, social media manager, freelancer</p><a href="#enquiry" data-c="Digital Marketing">Enquire about this course</a></details>
<details class="c"><summary><h3>Digital Rise</h3><p>Essential digital skills for the online world, in one course.</p></summary><img src="data:image/jpeg;base64," alt="Digital Rise course banner, ICCE Computer Education" style="width:100%;height:auto;border-radius:10px;display:block;margin-top:14px"><div class="ex"><div class="exp"><b>About this course</b><p>The Digital Rise program gives beginners the essential skills to use the digital world with confidence. It covers computer and internet basics, safe online payments and fraud awareness, productivity tools such as MS Office and Google tools, and simple design and content tools.</p><p>Students also learn ways to earn online, such as freelancing and selling online.</p><p>The goal is to make every student digitally confident and ready for work or a small online business.</p></div></div><b>Course syllabus</b><b class="mod">1. Computer &amp; Internet Basics</b><ul><li><strong>Using a computer:</strong> Windows, files and folders, typing.</li><li><strong>Internet &amp; email:</strong> Browsing, searching and creating an email account.</li><li><strong>Mobile &amp; apps:</strong> Using useful apps and online services.</li></ul><b class="mod">2. Online Safety &amp; Digital Payments</b><ul><li><strong>Digital payments:</strong> Using UPI and online banking safely.</li><li><strong>Safe browsing:</strong> Strong passwords and protecting personal information.</li><li><strong>Fraud awareness:</strong> Spotting fake messages, calls and links.</li><li><strong>Online government services:</strong> Using official websites for common services.</li></ul><b class="mod">3. Productivity Tools</b><ul><li><strong>MS Office:</strong> Word, Excel and PowerPoint for everyday work.</li><li><strong>Google tools:</strong> Docs, Sheets, Drive and Meet.</li><li><strong>Typing practice:</strong> Building speed and accuracy.</li></ul><b class="mod">4. Content &amp; Design Tools</b><ul><li><strong>Canva:</strong> Designing posters, resumes and social media posts.</li><li><strong>Photo and video editing:</strong> Basic editing with mobile and computer apps.</li><li><strong>Social media profiles:</strong> Setting up and managing profiles professionally.</li></ul><b class="mod">5. Earning Online</b><ul><li><strong>Freelancing:</strong> Finding online work and getting started on freelance platforms.</li><li><strong>Online selling:</strong> Selling products or services online.</li><li><strong>AI tools for work:</strong> Using AI tools to save time.</li></ul><b>Who it is for</b><p>Beginners who want to enter the digital world</p><b>Career options</b><p>Online work, freelancing, starting a small business online</p><a href="#enquiry" data-c="Digital Rise">Enquire about this course</a></details>
<details class="c"><summary><h3>DIT</h3><p>Diploma in Information Technology: a strong IT foundation with practical work.</p></summary><img src="data:image/jpeg;base64," alt="DIT course banner, ICCE Computer Education" style="width:100%;height:auto;border-radius:10px;display:block;margin-top:14px"><div class="ex"><div class="exp"><b>About this course</b><p>The DIT (Diploma in Information Technology) program builds a strong foundation in computers and technology. It starts with computer fundamentals and MS Office, then covers internet and networking basics, programming basics and web design.</p><p>Students practice with small projects to build confidence.</p><p>The goal is to prepare students for entry-level computer and office jobs and for further learning.</p></div></div><b>Course syllabus</b><b class="mod">1. Computer Fundamentals</b><ul><li><strong>Hardware &amp; software:</strong> Parts of a computer and how they work together.</li><li><strong>Operating system:</strong> Using Windows, files, settings and troubleshooting basics.</li><li><strong>Typing:</strong> Building typing speed and accuracy.</li></ul><b class="mod">2. MS Office</b><ul><li><strong>MS Word:</strong> Documents, formatting, tables and mail merge.</li><li><strong>MS Excel:</strong> Formulas, functions, charts and data handling.</li><li><strong>MS PowerPoint:</strong> Making clear and attractive presentations.</li></ul><b class="mod">3. Internet &amp; Networking Basics</b><ul><li><strong>Internet &amp; email:</strong> Browsing, searching and professional email use.</li><li><strong>Networking concepts:</strong> LAN, WAN, routers and how devices connect.</li><li><strong>Basic troubleshooting:</strong> Fixing common computer and network problems.</li></ul><b class="mod">4. Programming Basics</b><ul><li><strong>Logic &amp; flowcharts:</strong> Thinking step by step to solve problems.</li><li><strong>Programming language basics:</strong> Variables, conditions, loops and functions.</li><li><strong>Small projects:</strong> Practice programs to build confidence.</li></ul><b class="mod">5. Web Design Basics</b><ul><li><strong>HTML:</strong> Structure of a web page.</li><li><strong>CSS:</strong> Colours, fonts and layout.</li><li><strong>Simple website:</strong> Building and publishing a basic website.</li></ul><b>Who it is for</b><p>Those who want an IT career after 12th</p><b>Career options</b><p>Computer operator, IT support, office jobs</p><a href="#enquiry" data-c="DIT">Enquire about this course</a></details>
<details class="c"><summary><h3>DCA</h3><p>Diploma in Computer Applications: start with MS Office, internet and computer basics.</p></summary><img src="data:image/jpeg;base64," alt="DCA course banner, ICCE Computer Education" style="width:100%;height:auto;border-radius:10px;display:block;margin-top:14px"><div class="ex"><div class="exp"><b>About this course</b><p>The DCA (Diploma in Computer Applications) program is a complete beginner course for using computers in daily work. It covers computer fundamentals, MS Office (Word, Excel, PowerPoint), internet and email, accounting basics with Tally, and design basics.</p><p>Students practice typing and daily office tasks.</p><p>The goal is to make students confident computer users, ready for office and data entry work.</p></div></div><b>Course syllabus</b><b class="mod">1. Computer Fundamentals</b><ul><li><strong>Hardware &amp; software:</strong> Parts of a computer and what they do.</li><li><strong>Operating system:</strong> Using Windows, files and folders.</li><li><strong>Typing:</strong> Building typing speed and accuracy.</li></ul><b class="mod">2. MS Office</b><ul><li><strong>MS Word:</strong> Documents, formatting and tables.</li><li><strong>MS Excel:</strong> Formulas, functions and charts.</li><li><strong>MS PowerPoint:</strong> Creating presentations.</li></ul><b class="mod">3. Internet &amp; Email</b><ul><li><strong>Internet:</strong> Browsing and searching safely.</li><li><strong>Email:</strong> Creating accounts, sending files and attachments.</li><li><strong>Online forms:</strong> Filling common online forms correctly.</li></ul><b class="mod">4. Accounting Basics</b><ul><li><strong>Tally:</strong> Entering vouchers and maintaining accounts.</li><li><strong>Billing &amp; reports:</strong> Making bills and reading basic reports.</li><li><strong>GST basics:</strong> Introduction to GST in daily accounting.</li></ul><b class="mod">5. Design Basics</b><ul><li><strong>Introduction to design software:</strong> Photoshop or CorelDRAW basics.</li><li><strong>Simple designs:</strong> Creating visiting cards and posters.</li></ul><b>Who it is for</b><p>Beginners, 10th/12th pass students</p><b>Career options</b><p>Data entry, computer operator, office assistant</p><a href="#enquiry" data-c="DCA">Enquire about this course</a></details>
<details class="c"><summary><h3>DCAC</h3><p>Computer applications with career skills: learn the work and get job-ready.</p></summary><img src="data:image/jpeg;base64," alt="DCAC course banner, ICCE Computer Education" style="width:100%;height:auto;border-radius:10px;display:block;margin-top:14px"><div class="ex"><div class="exp"><b>About this course</b><p>The DCAC program combines computer applications with career skills. Students learn computer basics, MS Office, internet and email, and typing and data entry.</p><p>They also learn resume writing, interview preparation and communication skills.</p><p>The goal is to make students job-ready.</p></div></div><b>Course syllabus</b><b class="mod">1. Fundamentals of Computers</b><ul><li><strong>Computer basics:</strong> Hardware, software and Windows.</li><li><strong>Files &amp; folders:</strong> Saving, organising and finding your work.</li></ul><b class="mod">2. MS Office</b><ul><li><strong>MS Word:</strong> Documents, formatting and tables.</li><li><strong>MS Excel:</strong> Formulas, functions and charts.</li><li><strong>MS PowerPoint:</strong> Creating presentations.</li></ul><b class="mod">3. Internet, Email &amp; Online Forms</b><ul><li><strong>Internet &amp; email:</strong> Browsing, email accounts and attachments.</li><li><strong>Online forms:</strong> Filling and submitting forms correctly.</li></ul><b class="mod">4. Typing &amp; Data Entry</b><ul><li><strong>Typing practice:</strong> Speed and accuracy.</li><li><strong>Data entry:</strong> Entering data neatly and without mistakes.</li></ul><b class="mod">5. Career Skills</b><ul><li><strong>Resume writing:</strong> Making a clear, professional resume.</li><li><strong>Interview preparation:</strong> Common questions and how to answer them.</li><li><strong>Communication:</strong> Speaking and writing with confidence at work.</li></ul><b>Who it is for</b><p>Beginners, 10th/12th pass students, anyone looking for a job or office work</p><b>Career options</b><p>Data entry, computer operator, office assistant, back office jobs</p><a href="#enquiry" data-c="DCAC">Enquire about this course</a></details>
